.json` gains `latest.vtsr_c_*` trend fields + `latest_detail.vtsr_c` / `latest_detail.axis_outcome` blocks consumed absent-safely by the ELO page's Does-it-work tab. Smoke-run on current corpus (100 rated matches, 35 players, 30 clean_wins): pooled Spearman ρ = 0.462, self-consistency ρ = 0.804, calibration MAE = 0.018, **synthetic-winner agreement = 93.3% PASSES**, `clean_win` prediction accuracy: mean R 43.3% / **hard MAX R 53.3%** / softmax MAX R 46.7% (Dehpanah +10pp lift directionally confirmed; CIs overlap so not yet decisive), commander breakout degenerate (30/30 clean_wins have a commander — hypothesis untestable on current corpus), rating-gap breakout reframes the headline (0/30 matches have R-gap > 100; rating's predictive power untested at scale), bootstrap top-20 Jaccard = 0.826, rating-proxy σ ≈ 27 ELO median, axis ablation shows `snipe_bonus` + `target_lock_pct` lowest-impact (drop-rho 0.999 / 0.994), Dirichlet ρ = 0.986 mean (no knife-edge tuning). Full design + sequencing context: `critique/elo-analysis-v2.md` §5.1 + §6.1 + §9.
- **VTSR-C** (Commander Rating, v1 — experimental): `scripts/elo_commander.py` (pure module mirroring the `elo.py` contract; `compute_commander_elo(all_match_data, elo_history)` → `data/processed/elo_commander_current.json` + `elo_commander_history.json`, own `schema_version: 1`, both in the `load_cache_index()` skip set). **Outcome-pure (`α_c = 1`) win/loss ELO between the two commanders of every DETERMINED rated match** (`decided_by` ∈ adjudicated/attested/clean_win/contested with `winner.team` ∈ {1,2}; attested/adjudicated draws score 0.5 both) with a **team-strength handicap** in the expected score: `E_A = 1/(1+10^(−((R_A−R_B)+λ(T_A−T_B))/400))` where `T` = mean pre-match VTSR-T of each team's non-commander rated rows from the canonical `elo_history` deltas' `before` values (zero leakage) and `λ = CMDR_LAMBDA_TEAM_HANDICAP = 1.0` (validator-ablated). Classic chess constants where W/L semantics differ from VTSR-T's performance semantics: logistic scale 400 (not 800), symmetric K 40 → 20 over the first 5 duels (no loss aversion — zero-sum), no rating floor, anchor 1500, provisional badge below 5 rated games. **Corpus-wide, picker-unaware, NOT in the pipeline cache key; the dashboard thug-only toggle does NOT apply (separate ladder). Experimental posture** — provisional-heavy labeling, visible game counts, "experimental" tags. No `PIPELINE_VERSION` / `ELO_SCHEMA_VERSION` / `match.schema_version` interaction (recomputes every run). Consumers (all 404-safe): ELO page ladder card + all four explainer pills, dashboard Commander Cohort top-5 strip (`ensureCommanderEloLoaded()` in `js/app.js`), player-page Commander Rivalries panel (`js/player.js` computes per-opponent tallies client-side from its contributions walk — the aggregator's `head_to_head` is capped at top-10 globally). Roadmap: performance axes join via `α_c` when commander telemetry lands. Full derivation: `DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md` §13.12; schemas: `docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md` §11.
- Client-side All Matches aggregator: `js/all-matches-aggregator.js` (pure `VTAggregate.build(contributions, fileIds)` summation over `data/processed/match_contributions.json`; mirrors what `scripts/process_stats.py` `build_all_matches_aggregate()` used to produce, but folds in only the subset of file ids that pass the active picker facet filter). Loaded after `js/positioning-player.js` in `index.html`, before `js/app.js`.
- Picker filter contract: the match-picker modal (`#match-picker-modal`) carries facets — duration band, player count, submitter, full-roster Players (with Match-mode `any of these` / `all of these` and Role `any` / `Commander` / `Thug`). State is `pickerState` in `js/app.js`, persisted in sessionStorage under `vt.picker.filters.v2` (one-shot v1 migration on first read). The All Matches card subtitle, the All-Matches view's filter banner, and the trigger subtitles all update from `applyPickerFilters()`; when the user is on the All Matches view, a debounced `loadAllMatches()` rerun re-aggregates from cached contributions so the career table / radar / global meta reflect the new subset.
- Sentinel damage reference: `docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md` §7 "Sentinel Damage Filter" (full evidence chain + decompile + struct layout for the `DAMAGE_TYPE_UNKNOWN` force-kill pathway; linked from rules + DEVELOPER_GUIDE). UnitDestroyed four-way classification + powerup economy reference: same dictionary §8.
- Team faction detection (ISDF / Hadean / Scion): `detect_team_factions()` in `scripts/process_stats.py` derives each team's faction from per-slot ODF first-letter votes (Algorithm A: starting-ship `PlayerState.odf` per slot; Algorithm B: event-stream votes from every team-attributed vehicle/structure/pilot ODF). Output at `match.team_factions = {"1": {"code", "name"} | null, "2": ...}`, sibling to `team_leaders`. Match-global, always-unfiltered. Bumped `match.schema_version` from 2 to 3. Faction badges render via `.vt-faction-badge[data-faction-code]` in `css/vtstats-theme.css` next to team-leader names in `renderFactionScoreboard()`. Full per-source vote table + edge cases: `docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md` §9.
- Match winner resolution: `resolve_match_outcome(raw_game_outcome, kill_feed)` in `scripts/process_stats.py` combines the proto v3 host attestation with the `compute_match_winner(kill_feed)` toggle-model inference through an evidence-first trust ladder (v15: attested `GAME_CANCELLED` always wins → a `clean_win` inference beats a contradicting attestation, flagged `disputed: true` → attested team wins/draws resolve contested/unclear → no attestation = inference verbatim). Final `decided_by` ∈ `adjudicated` / `attested` / `clean_win` / `contested` / `unclear` / `draw` / `cancelled`; `team` / `loser` are `null` for the last three. **v16 — human adjudication (precedence level 0)**: every proto v3+ match prompts once during `python scripts/process_stats.py` (console: teams with canonical Steam names + `[aka "nick"]` hints, leaders, host choice, evidence, memory joggers; options `1/2/3/4` mirror the collector dialog + `Enter` confirm / `u` unknown / `d` defer) — answers persist in the committed `data/match_outcome_adjudications.json` (keyed by match id, flushed per answer, human-editable with automatic reconciliation) and are applied by `scripts/adjudication.py::apply_outcome` as pure winner-block rewrites (confirmations keep the original `decided_by` + set `adjudicated: true`; overrides set `decided_by: "adjudicated"`). Pipeline flags: `--no-prompt` (automation — REQUIRED for CI or it hangs on stdin), `--force-prompt` (piped-stdin testing), `--adjudicate-all` (legacy backfill). Manifest mirrors `winner_decided_by` + `winner_adjudicated`. Renderer (`renderKillFeed()` in `js/app.js`) injects a `.vt-winner-badge[data-decided-by]` in the Kill Feed card header (tooltips on all provenance states; warning glyph on disputed; `bi-check2-circle` check-mark on reviewer-signed-off matches), highlights the winning team's `.vt-faction-panel` with `.vt-faction-panel--winner`, and inserts an in-feed `.vt-killfeed-milestone` divider at `decided_at_tick`. **Filter-safe**: read winner from `currentData.match.winner`, never from the (filterable) `kills.feed`. Full trust-ladder + adjudication reference: `docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md` §10.
